[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186124608 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f854dc07-e895-544c-8c1b-b7252e458077"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f854dc07-e895-544c-8c1b-b7252e458077" :question/id #uuid "f854dc07-e895-544c-8c1b-b7252e458077" :question/math-academy-id "q-98334" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(0,3)=8,\\,{f}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{4{e}^{2x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+y}},\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+y}}.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,3),$ estimate the value of $f(-0.05,2.9).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(0,3)+∇f(0,3)\\cdot ⟨x-0,y-3⟩ \\\\  & =f(0,3)+⟨{f}_{x}(0,3),{f}_{y}(0,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y-3⟩ \\\\  & =8+⟨{f}_{x}(0,3),{f}_{y}(0,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(0,3)$ and ${f}_{y}(0,3)$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,3) & =\\frac{4{e}^{2(0)}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2(0)}+3}}=2 \\\\ {f}_{y}(0,3) & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2(0)}+3}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈8+⟨2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y-3⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(-0.05,2.9)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=-0.05$ and $y=2.9,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.05,2.9) & ≈8+⟨2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.05,2.9-3⟩ \\\\  & =8+⟨2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.05,-0.1⟩ \\\\  & =8-0.1-0.1 \\\\  & =7.8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64595e8b-79ea-579b-9327-3bae1f493628"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64595e8b-79ea-579b-9327-3bae1f493628" :answer-field/id #uuid "64595e8b-79ea-579b-9327-3bae1f493628" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-50c8d8e4-0e18-5b33-b84b-54f0e515991d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-89972dfd-4748-5c03-b875-261477bf4e9c" "answer-15bf8319-f568-5e0b-9738-a8834dd0a9bb" "answer-50c8d8e4-0e18-5b33-b84b-54f0e515991d" "answer-446ca39e-c464-566a-b2c4-b84b42d9500c" "answer-720d7d75-c88a-510f-8b1b-79e165c0a1a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89972dfd-4748-5c03-b875-261477bf4e9c" :answer/id #uuid "89972dfd-4748-5c03-b875-261477bf4e9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15bf8319-f568-5e0b-9738-a8834dd0a9bb" :answer/id #uuid "15bf8319-f568-5e0b-9738-a8834dd0a9bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50c8d8e4-0e18-5b33-b84b-54f0e515991d" :answer/id #uuid "50c8d8e4-0e18-5b33-b84b-54f0e515991d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-446ca39e-c464-566a-b2c4-b84b42d9500c" :answer/id #uuid "446ca39e-c464-566a-b2c4-b84b42d9500c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-720d7d75-c88a-510f-8b1b-79e165c0a1a9" :answer/id #uuid "720d7d75-c88a-510f-8b1b-79e165c0a1a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-f854dc07-e895-544c-8c1b-b7252e458077" :question/id #uuid "f854dc07-e895-544c-8c1b-b7252e458077"] ["question-f854dc07-e895-544c-8c1b-b7252e458077" :question/math-academy-id "q-98334"] ["question-f854dc07-e895-544c-8c1b-b7252e458077" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(0,3)=8,\\,{f}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{4{e}^{2x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+y}},\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+y}}.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,3),$ estimate the value of $f(-0.05,2.9).$"] ["question-f854dc07-e895-544c-8c1b-b7252e458077" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(0,3)+∇f(0,3)\\cdot ⟨x-0,y-3⟩ \\\\  & =f(0,3)+⟨{f}_{x}(0,3),{f}_{y}(0,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y-3⟩ \\\\  & =8+⟨{f}_{x}(0,3),{f}_{y}(0,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(0,3)$ and ${f}_{y}(0,3)$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,3) & =\\frac{4{e}^{2(0)}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2(0)}+3}}=2 \\\\ {f}_{y}(0,3) & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2(0)}+3}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈8+⟨2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y-3⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(-0.05,2.9)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=-0.05$ and $y=2.9,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.05,2.9) & ≈8+⟨2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.05,2.9-3⟩ \\\\  & =8+⟨2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.05,-0.1⟩ \\\\  & =8-0.1-0.1 \\\\  & =7.8\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-f854dc07-e895-544c-8c1b-b7252e458077" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-64595e8b-79ea-579b-9327-3bae1f493628" :answer-field/id #uuid "64595e8b-79ea-579b-9327-3bae1f493628"] ["answer-89972dfd-4748-5c03-b875-261477bf4e9c" :answer/id #uuid "89972dfd-4748-5c03-b875-261477bf4e9c"] ["answer-89972dfd-4748-5c03-b875-261477bf4e9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-89972dfd-4748-5c03-b875-261477bf4e9c" :answer/value "7.6"] ["answer-15bf8319-f568-5e0b-9738-a8834dd0a9bb" :answer/id #uuid "15bf8319-f568-5e0b-9738-a8834dd0a9bb"] ["answer-15bf8319-f568-5e0b-9738-a8834dd0a9bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-15bf8319-f568-5e0b-9738-a8834dd0a9bb" :answer/value "7.75"] ["answer-50c8d8e4-0e18-5b33-b84b-54f0e515991d" :answer/id #uuid "50c8d8e4-0e18-5b33-b84b-54f0e515991d"] ["answer-50c8d8e4-0e18-5b33-b84b-54f0e515991d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-50c8d8e4-0e18-5b33-b84b-54f0e515991d" :answer/value "7.8"] ["answer-446ca39e-c464-566a-b2c4-b84b42d9500c" :answer/id #uuid "446ca39e-c464-566a-b2c4-b84b42d9500c"] ["answer-446ca39e-c464-566a-b2c4-b84b42